---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Run a read-only contract call (an evm-call request file, or --to, --abi and --function) and print the decoded result or revert

Usage: rustman evm call [OPTIONS] [REQUEST|ARG]...

Arguments:
  [REQUEST|ARG]...
          An evm-call request (file, id or name); with --to, the function's arguments instead

Options:
      --to <ADDRESS>
          The contract: an address or ENS name (an ad-hoc call)

      --abi <ABI>
          The ABI of an ad-hoc call: erc20, erc721, erc1155 or a path from the workspace root

      --function <FUNCTION>
          The function of an ad-hoc call: a name or a full signature

      --block <BLOCK>
          The block: latest, finalized, a number or a hash (ad-hoc calls)

      --from <ADDRESS>
          The caller address (ad-hoc calls)

      --value <AMOUNT>
          The value sent with the call, such as "1 ether" (ad-hoc calls)

      --estimate
          Also report eth_estimateGas for the same call

      --trace
          Also print the call tree (debug_traceCall, then trace_call)

      --no-history
          Do not record the call in history

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --rpc <URL>
          The node: a URL or a {{variable}} (default: the environment's {{rpc}})

      --var <K=V>
          Set a variable, above every other source (repeatable): --var k=v

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Total timeout per node call: 500ms, 5s, 2m, or milliseconds

  -k, --insecure
          Do not verify TLS certificates

      --json
          Print one JSON object instead of text

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
